\p{Field note from the Neuromodulation Conference (NYC, 2026), filed under [[conf-neuromod-nyc-2026]]. This is the flagship \strong{sense stimulation & distinct qualia} talk: Robert Gaunt's RNEL group runs \strong{bidirectional} BCIs — motor decoding out, and intracortical microstimulation (ICMS) of somatosensory cortex back in — where stimulation on a given electrode evokes a \strong{distinct, localized tactile percept} on the hand. That evoked percept is the quale; the "last a decade" framing is about array longevity holding that percept map stable over years.}

\subtree{\title{Title}
\taxon{remark}
